{
  "id": "osm_nav",
  "title": "Navigation",
  "description": "Offline OpenStreetMap navigation for Georgia (Georgian and English) in place of the BMW map, in iDrive 7's own look: GPU map in the BMW map's style, the car's own menus and lists, turn-by-turn guidance, the next turn on the head-up display (with cluster-render), the car's GPS where the firmware gives it, speed limits, and the console's NAV button. Experimental: not tested in a car.",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "vendor": "custom",
  "loggingId": "OANV",
  "iconGlyph": "nav",
  "mguInternet": false,
  "replacesStockNav": true,
  "startWidget": {
    "name": "Navigation",
    "layout": "LT_Table_OnlineApps_DriveRecorderWidget",
    "image": "BackgroundImage1",
    "cells": {
      "HeadlineText": [
        "Navigation",
        "Text"
      ]
    }
  },
  "mguHmi": [
    "ID7"
  ],
  "nativeSettingsComment": "nativeSettings: the settings open as the HMI's own list (BMW's look and focus) also where the kit runs the screen; NAV_MENU and NAV_LIST are native lists too (setting \"menus\"): while one is open the drawn screen hides and the controller is the HMI's.",
  "nativeSettings": true,
  "maxDiskUsage": 268435456,
  "mapsComment": "The map, kept out of git (hexlay/idrive7-geo-map-data releases): kit/tools/build.py downloads it (once, into kit/tools/.osm-cache), checks its size and SHA-256 and puts it into the package unpacked. A new map: a new release there and its numbers here.",
